\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The exclusion ladder. Each row is a population defined by which alternative-explanation classes are removed, with the replacement median and the collapse count computed on that population alone. These are six descriptions of six samples and not six estimates of one quantity: the rows differ in which events they contain, not in how an estimand is computed, and the differences between them are the sensitivity of the pooled figures to the audit rather than a causal measure of anything. The fourth row removes only the explanations whose record is market-wide or names the firm and the formulation.}}{24}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ladder}{{10}{24}{The exclusion ladder. Each row is a population defined by which alternative-explanation classes are removed, with the replacement median and the collapse count computed on that population alone. These are six descriptions of six samples and not six estimates of one quantity: the rows differ in which events they contain, not in how an estimand is computed, and the differences between them are the sensitivity of the pooled figures to the audit rather than a causal measure of anything. The fourth row removes only the explanations whose record is market-wide or names the firm and the formulation}{table.10}{}}
